{%- doc -%}
  One card in a reassurance row: a glyph, a title and a line of copy. Renders
  [ui-feature-card] and nothing else, for the reason [_ui-product-chip] gives — the
  look belongs to the kit and this is the merchant's handle on it.

  It is a block rather than a run of settings on the section so a page can show two
  claims or five, in any order, without the section growing a `case` for each. That
  is the rule `docs/section-settings.md` opens with.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign card_icon = block.settings.icon
  if card_icon == 'none'
    assign card_icon = ''
  endif
-%}

{%- if block.settings.title != blank or block.settings.body != blank -%}
  <div class="ui-feature-card-block" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    {%- comment -%}
      The pill straddling the card's top edge on a numbered row. It belongs to the
      wrapper rather than to [ui-feature-card] because it is not part of what that
      card is — it is the row saying which of its cards this one is, and a card
      standing on its own never wears one.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if block.settings.badge != blank -%}
      <span class="ui-feature-card-block__badge">{{ block.settings.badge }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}

    {% render 'ui-feature-card',
      icon: card_icon,
      title: block.settings.title,
      body: block.settings.body
    %}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
   * The wrapper the editor needs for its outline has to pass the grid cell through
   * in both directions: its width, or a long line of copy sets its own and the
   * columns stop matching, and its height, or the card inside cannot fill the row.
   */
  .ui-feature-card-block {
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }

  /*
   * Centred on the card's top edge and lifted by half its own height, so it sits
   * across the edge the way the file draws it whatever the badge's height is.
   */
  .ui-feature-card-block__badge {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-start: 0;
    inset-inline: 0;
    z-index: 1;
    inline-size: fit-content;
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: 4px 8px;
    border-radius: var(--ui-radius-sm);
    background-color: var(--ui-color-primary);
    color: var(--ui-color-white);
    font-family: var(--ui-font-accent);
    font-weight: var(--font-accent--weight-semibold, 600);
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 1.35;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
  }

  .ui-feature-card-block > .ui-feature-card {
    inline-size: 100%;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

